ask to what extent these traditions have been maintained or transformed in the face of market liberalization and integration within the European Union.\u00a0The class is organized in three parts. In part one, we will discuss major 'national models', including Germany, the Nordic countries, and France \u2013 reviewing both the history of these models and recent changes in collective bargaining and labor market institutions. In part two, we will compare major areas of labor market policy across European countries, including pay, parental leave, gender quotas, employment protection, and working time flexibility. In part three, we will examine the process and politics of European integration in the European Union (EU), including extension into Central and Eastern European countries and migration within Europe. The class will conclude with a discussion of challenges facing the EU: support for far right parties; responses to the climate crisis; and geopolitical conflict.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 370745, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRIC", "catalogNbr": "4337", "titleShort": "Labor and Employment in the Mi", "titleLong": "Labor and Employment in the Middle East and North Africa", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 17901, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:00PM", "timeEnd": "02:15PM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "db833", "firstName": "Dina", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Bishara"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Ives Hall 111", "bldgDescr": "Ives Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "IVS111", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "ILRIC", "catalogNbr": "6337", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "NES", "catalogNbr": "4337", "type": "B"}, {"subject": "NES", "catalogNbr": "6337", "type": "B"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course introduces students to the history, evolution and trajectory of state-labor relations, labor activism, and the politics of unemployment in the Middle East and North Africa (MENA). As the region with the highest concentration of non-democratic regimes in the world, the MENA provides a rich context for examining state efforts to control interest representation, and workers' struggles for freedom of association. In addition, the region features diverse political economic systems, making it ideal for examining the interaction between resource endowments and labor market dynamics. Finally, the region is ripe for the study of youth activism and the mobilization of the unemployed given that youth unemployment rates are higher in the MENA than any other world region.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 371383, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRIC", "catalogNbr": "4940", "titleShort": "ILR Global Scholars Capstone", "titleLong": "ILR Global Scholars Capstone", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 11263, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:20AM", "timeEnd": "12:10PM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "edf48", "firstName": "Eli", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Friedman"}], "pattern": "M", "facilityDescr": "Ives Hall 107", "bldgDescr": "Ives Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "IVS107", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1, "unitsMaximum": 1, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "SUI", "gradingBasisShort": "S/U NoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This capstone course is open to ILR Global Scholars (GS) during their last semester of their senior year. The course is designed for GS to incorporate their education and experience abroad with the concepts and theories they have gained while at the ILR School. The overarching goal of this class is to bring GS together to collectively reflect on and identify key aspects of intercultural competency related to their personal and cultural growth, academic and professional development and roles as future global citizens. The structure of the course will be group discussions, peer review, and individual reflection papers. The final capstone reflection paper will fulfill the course requirement and the Global Scholars Program final reflection requirement.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: students participating in the ILR Global Scholars program.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 367770, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRIC", "catalogNbr": "5300", "titleShort": "HR and Outsourcing in the Netw", "titleLong": "Human Resources and Outsourcing in the Networked Firm", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 17899, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:25AM", "timeEnd": "12:40PM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "vld7", "firstName": "Virginia", "middleName": "L", "lastName": "Doellgast"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Ives Hall 112", "bldgDescr": "Ives Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "IVS112", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course examines outsourcing decisions from a human resources perspective, and the human resource implications of managing workers in increasingly networked organizations. Outsourcing, offshoring, spin-offs, and the use of temporary staffing agencies all create challenges for human resource management. Firms face issues of retaining employee knowledge and skills, coordinating HR policies across multiple subcontractors, and motivating workers on different employment contracts \u2013 who in some cases work together within a workplace or virtually. In addition, organizations face increasingly complex decisions concerning the mix of sourcing strategies to use for their own HR functions and processes. The quality and content of these decisions have implications for performance outcomes, as well as for job quality and employee careers. We will analyze these challenges and evaluate strategies to address them from a comparative and international perspective, using industry- and firm-based case studies from North America, Europe, and Asia. The course will end with a discussion of current and future trends, including crowdsourcing, managing the human cloud, and the sharing economy. Some sample company case studies include Boeing, P&amp;G, Toyota, and IKEA.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "IL", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 369286, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRIC", "catalogNbr": "5555", "titleShort": "Leadership Development Skills", "titleLong": "Leadership Development Skills", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 20024, "meetings": [], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "DUBLIN", "locationDescr": "Dublin, Ireland", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "D", "addConsentDescr": "Department Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCod